Critical Ollama GPU Note (important)

If you install Ollama in /workspace by extracting only the binary, GPU inference may silently fall back to CPU.

Reason:

- /workspace/ollama/bin/ollama alone is not enough for CUDA inference
- GPU runners/libraries are required under lib/ollama
- in this setup they exist at /usr/local/lib/ollama

So after creating /workspace/ollama, also do:

mkdir -p /workspace/ollama/lib
ln -s /usr/local/lib/ollama /workspace/ollama/lib/ollama

Then run Ollama with models path on /workspace:

OLLAMA_MODELS=/workspace/ollama/models OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11434 /workspace/ollama/bin/ollama serve

Verification:

- check log for "inference compute ... library=CUDA"
- if it shows "library=cpu", GPU runners are still not being used

Example:

cd /workspace
mkdir ollama
mkdir models

From now on, treat /workspace as your real machine disk.

You are now in stable infrastructure mode.

